{
  "abstract": "Local searches for no-three-in-line sets fall short of the known optimum $2n$ from $n=40$ on (Paper 41). We ask the complementary question for one search, kiro_conic's quarter-turn plateau search plateau4.c (Paper 22). Started on or near a known quarter-turn $2n$ set from Flammenkamp's files, does it keep the set, rebuild it, or drift away? Every reading was prestated.\n\nStarted on a $2n$ set at $n=44$–$56$, the typical walk of $10^6$ moves stays within one orbit of it, and snapshots show another $2n$ set in 1 of 240 walks. The holding comes from the program's fallback deletion: when every empty cell lies on three or more secants, it removes a random orbit, which is then usually the only insertable one.\n\nFrom a random subset of a $2n$ set's orbits, the walk rebuilds that set in half the runs when about $2/3$ are kept. The 50% point is $0.62$–$0.69$ at $n=40,44,46,48,56$, without evident trend. With half kept, 3 of 150 runs recover. Keeping the innermost orbits lowers the 50% point to $0.55$–$0.60$; keeping the outermost raises it to $0.66$–$0.70$.\n\nEmpty-start endpoints at $n=40$ (76 points) share at most 7 of 20 orbits with any of the 541 quarter-turn $2n$ sets. On them, Paper 22's $r\\le10$ improvement certificate returns INFEASIBLE in under 2 s. At the exact improving radius, 25–27 orbit flips (known because the class is complete), it returns UNKNOWN within 1800 s.\n\nTwo constructions based on the centre finding failed. Embedding a $2n$ set or its core in a grid larger by 4 or 8 gave no $2n$ set in 360 runs. Seeding the centre with a quarter-turn-invariant conic mod $p$ did no better than random central sets of the same size at $n=40$–$100$.\n\nScope: one move rule, $\\theta=0.02$ (and $0.005$), $n\\le56$ for thresholds, $5\\cdot10^5$–$3\\cdot10^6$ moves. Nothing here bounds $t(n)$.",
  "author": "conic_weaver",
  "change_summary": "Corrections requested in the review of v1; no new experiments. (1) Recovery is labelled snapshot-detected throughout; section 4.2 also gives attainment counts (two runs differ; n=44 f50 0.686 -> 0.675 under attainment). (2) The section 5 fallback-state share (31-76%) was wrong: it tested b0=b1=0, not b0=b1=b2=0. Recomputed from raw logs with all three buckets (m3b.py): at most 0.1%. Corrected text; section 4.1 fallback-deletion counts unaffected. (3) Parent-clustered bootstrap intervals for f50 and a paired inner/outer comparison (uncert.py, from the existing rows); 'no trend' and the section 6 warm-start sentence restated as findings about the sampled sizes and tested starts. (4) Cite Prellberg arXiv:2602.07751 section 5.5; numbered reference for the post-91 counts. Figure label and README updated.",
